  <!-- ============================================================
       A5: io.prometheus:simpleclient_tracer_otel_agent 0.16.0 — deprecated, transitive.
       CVE-2023-43810, CVE-2023-45142, CVE-2023-47108 (W3C Trace Context parsing in old otel API).
       Comes via Spring Boot/Quarkus actuator chains; not directly used by X-Road code.
       Superseded by Micrometer in current metrics path. Risk: parsing of inbound HTTP trace headers,
       which X-Road services do not forward to this code path.
       ============================================================ -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      io.prometheus:simpleclient_tracer_otel_agent 0.16.0 is the deprecated Prometheus simpleclient
      tracer bridge for the old OpenTelemetry Java API. Pulled transitively by actuator BOMs.
      X-Road services use Micrometer for metrics; this artifact is not on the runtime tracing path.
      CVE-2023-43810/45142/47108 are W3C TraceContext parsing issues that require the artifact to
      actively parse inbound trace headers — which is not invoked by any X-Road code path.
      Re-evaluate when upstream BOM (Spring Boot / Quarkus) stops pulling this transitive.
    ]]></notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.prometheus/simpleclient_tracer.*@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2023-43810</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2023-45142</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2023-47108</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!-- ============================================================
       E1: spring-cloud-vault-config 5.0.1 — no upstream patch yet.
       CVE-2026-40981 / 40982 / 41002. spring-cloud-vault highest published version is 5.0.1.
       Monitor https://github.com/spring-cloud/spring-cloud-vault for 5.0.2 / 5.1.0 release.
       ============================================================ -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      Spring Cloud Vault 5.0.1 (CVE-2026-40981, CVE-2026-40982, CVE-2026-41002) — accepted risk.
      No upstream patch available as of 2026-05-25; 5.0.1 is the latest published version,
      and the parent BOM (spring-cloud 2025.1.1) is already on the latest stable release line.
      Mitigations in place: Vault access restricted to localhost socket inside containerised security-server;
      no untrusted HTTP input reaches the vault config client. Remove this suppression when
      Spring Cloud Vault 5.0.2 / 5.1.0 ships a fix.
    ]]></notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.cloud/spring-cloud-(vault-config|starter-vault-config)@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-40981</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2026-40982</cve>
    <cve>CVE-2026-41002</cve>
  </suppress>

